From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pmic_glink_altmode: defer for late mux only on SM8750

ROCKNIX carries this in its SM8750 kernel: the Odin 3 and Pocket FIT
Elite mode-switch supplier (the wcd_usbss SBU switch on I2C) registers
after pmic_glink_altmode probes, so a NULL mux there means not-yet and
running without it permanently loses SBU/DP-AUX routing. Armada ships
one kernel for every SoC, and boards that declare no mode-switch at all
(the AYANEO SM8550 family) make a NULL mux permanent; deferring on it
blocks the DP aux bridges, keeps the msm DRM aggregate from binding, and
the internal panel never lights. Gate the deferral to SM8750 so every
other SoC keeps the upstream tolerant behavior.

---
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -637,6 +637,17 @@
 					     "failed to acquire mode-switch for port: %d\n",
 					     port);
 		}
+		/*
+		 * On SM8750 a NULL mux means the mode-switch supplier has not
+		 * registered yet; retry rather than run permanently without
+		 * SBU/DP-AUX routing. Other SoCs may not declare one at all.
+		 */
+		if (!alt_port->typec_mux && of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm8750")) {
+			fwnode_handle_put(fwnode);
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+					     "mode-switch not registered yet for port: %d\n",
+					     port);
+		}
 
 		ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, pmic_glink_altmode_put_mux,
 					       alt_port->typec_mux);
@@ -667,6 +678,13 @@
 					     "failed to acquire orientation-switch for port: %d\n",
 					     port);
 		}
+		if (!alt_port->typec_switch &&
+		    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm8750")) {
+			fwnode_handle_put(fwnode);
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+					     "orientation-switch not registered yet for port: %d\n",
+					     port);
+		}
 
 		ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, pmic_glink_altmode_put_switch,
 					       alt_port->typec_switch);
